Subject: winebus: keep SDL away from the PlayStation controllers winebus reads as raw HID.
Author: AnvilMac contributors (Claude Code), 2026-10-29
Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, same as Wine dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c.
Provenance: original change against Wine 11.19, source tarball
73eb0b02dfc0cb0ff4f4d8d36c5786261e9725ac91968ae4d4e4b9a498c4087f.
Not an upstream commit; not submitted upstream.

winebus.sys prefers raw HID for DualShock 4 and DualSense pads, so their SDL
devices are dropped, but only after SDL has opened them: its HIDAPI drivers set
the light bar, player lights and report mode, and its MFi path resets the player
index, while winebus reads the same pad (patches 0011 and 0012 rely on its mode).
Before SDL_Init, list Wine's DualShock 4 and DualSense ids in
SDL_GAMECONTROLLER_IGNORE_DEVICES: SDL's HIDAPI, IOKit and MFi paths all check
that list before touching a device (SDL 2.32.10 source, read 2026-10-29). Other
controllers (Xbox, Switch and others) go through SDL as before.

Tested 2026-10-29 with a local build including patches 0011-0013 and SDL 2.32.10:
SDL loaded and added no PlayStation device; the owner's PS4 and PS5 worked in
Unruly Heroes and Shank (including two players). No non-PlayStation pad was
available to test.
---
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
@@ -1073,6 +1073,7 @@
 
 NTSTATUS sdl_bus_init(void *args)
 {
+    typeof(SDL_SetHint) *set_hint;
     const char *mapping;
     int i;
 
@@ -1146,6 +1147,13 @@
     pSDL_JoystickGetVendor = dlsym(sdl_handle, "SDL_JoystickGetVendor");
     pSDL_JoystickGetType = dlsym(sdl_handle, "SDL_JoystickGetType");
     pSDL_JoystickGetSerial = dlsym(sdl_handle, "SDL_JoystickGetSerial");
+
+    /* PlayStation pads stay on the hidraw path, which winebus.sys prefers for them (is_dualshock4_gamepad,
+     * is_dualsense_gamepad). Keep SDL from adding them at all: its drivers would change their light bar, player
+     * lights and report mode while winebus reads them. */
+    if ((set_hint = dlsym(sdl_handle, "SDL_SetHint")))
+        set_hint(SDL_HINT_GAMECONTROLLER_IGNORE_DEVICES,
+                 "0x054c/0x05c4,0x054c/0x09cc,0x054c/0x0ba0,0x054c/0x0ce6,0x054c/0x0df2");
 
     if (pSDL_Init(SDL_INIT_GAMECONTROLLER | SDL_INIT_HAPTIC) < 0)
     {
